  "body": "## Result\n\nAdds a scoped, exact negative result for one symmetric ten-term P112 decoder. The pinned witness from PR1633 has support-rank invoice `(8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,9,9)`, total 82. The verifier exhausts every rational Householder gauge `O_s=I-2ss^T/(s^Ts)` for nonzero ternary normal `s in {-1,0,1}^10`, modulo sign: 29,524 candidates. All ten terms remain active, every exact P112 identity is preserved by the checked orthogonal numerator, and the candidates produce nine support-rank histograms, all using only ranks 8 and 9. The minimum invoice remains 82.\n\n## Cost screen and limits\n\nSubstituting the best ten-term support profile for the selected eight rank-8 centre children changes the centre mass from 64 to 82. Even with all coefficient, frame, precision, hosting, storage and restoration overhead waived, the exact selected-profile ceiling is in `[0.000834274164361244, 0.000834274164361245]`, below the selected fixed-word ceiling `0.001690054109089` and its 5% target `0.00177455681454345`. This closes only the searched Householder orbit of the one pinned symmetric witness. It is not a lower bound for all ten-term, asymmetric or other-support decoders; no supplier adoption or new `kappa` is claimed.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```sh\npython3 -B research/p112-householder-gauge-seed06ace/verify.py\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/p112-householder-gauge-seed06ace --check-only\n```\n\nThe direct verifier and package metadata/source-pin check pass locally under Python 3.14.7. The registered replay targets Python 3.12, unavailable locally; that replay remains for CI/reviewer confirmation.\n\n## Pins and credit\n\nSeed `06ace58bfc2b63b47b02129f729e35d4`; track `complex-mechanisms`; task `complex-rank-shape-decoder`; priority revision 3. Exact base `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`. Selected-record SHA-256 `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`. The selected review, source manifest, assembly certificate, and ceiling implementation are pinned in `SOURCES.json`.\n\nThe witness is from Hanson Sun's open PR1633 at head `652264fa1f70820139b2730363a0056b7fadc689`; its exact result artifact is pinned in `WITNESS.json` and `SOURCES.json`. The bounded claim and handoff are in [Discussion #1622 comment 18925227](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1622#discussioncomment-18925227). PR1224, PR1077 and PR968 are credited in the README. Substantial OpenAI Codex assistance is disclosed.\n",
